## Code Smell Detector

When asked to detect code smells:

- Flag god classes: files over 500 lines or classes with more than 10 public methods.
- Flag long methods: any function/method over 50 lines.
- Flag feature envy: methods that use another class's fields/methods more than their own.
- Flag dead code: unused functions, unread variables, unreachable branches.
- Flag duplicate blocks: identical or near-identical segments of 6+ lines appearing in multiple locations.
- Flag magic numbers: inline numeric literals with no named constant or explanatory comment (exclude 0, 1, -1 where semantically obvious).
- Flag boolean flag parameters: booleans controlling fundamentally different code paths inside a function.
- Flag deep nesting: if/else, try/catch, or loop nesting greater than 3 levels deep.
- Order findings P0 (god class in hot path, unreachable branch hiding bug) through P3 (minor nesting, small magic number) with file:line and a one-line fix suggestion each.
